	(text "Pin numbers (1-166) are PLACEHOLDERS for schematic netlist intent. Refine to actual BGA ball positions\n(A1, B2, ..., T16) via the Lattice pin-planner once banks / clock-capable pins / DDR pairing are decided.\n\nAll FP_*, VGA_*, HDMI_*, I2S_*, I2C_*, FP_SD_*, JTAG_*, CFG_* hierarchical labels are auto-named via\nKiCad's same-name net-merge with the labels at the U_FPGA pin endpoints below.\n\nDecoupling shown is representative; per ECP5 datasheet, place one 100nF per VCC ball + bulk caps at PCB layout."
